"111111011111000001100100000011100001111000111111111111":1,"111111011111000001100100000011111111111111001100001011":1,"111111011111001111100011110000000000000000000000000000":1,"111111011111001111100011110000011110000111000000000000":1,"111111011111001111100011110000111110001111000100001011":1,"111111011111001111100011110000111110001111110111111111":2,"111111011111001111100111110011000001110000001000000000":1,"111111011111001111100111110011011111110111001000000000":1,"111111011111001111100111110011011111110111111011110100":1,"111111011111001111100111110011100001111000001100001011":1,"111111011111001111100111110011100001111000111111111111":1,"111111011111001111100111110011111111111111001100001011":1,"111111011111001111100111110011111111111111111111111111":3,"111111111111110001111000001100000000000000000000000000":1,"111111111111110001111000001100000000000000110011110100":2,"111111111111110001111000001100011110000111110011110100":2,"111111111111110001111000001100111110001111110111111111":1,"111111111111110001111100001111000001110000001000000000":1,"111111111111110001111100001111000001110000111011110100":1,"111111111111110001111100001111011111110111001000000000":3,"111111111111110001111100001111111111111111001100001011":1,"111111111111110001111100001111111111111111111111111111":1,"111111111111111111111011111100000000000000000000000000":1,"111111111111111111111011111100000000000000110011110100":1,"111111111111111111111011111100011110000111110011110100":1,"111111111111111111111011111100100000001000000100001011":1,"111111111111111111111011111100100000001000110111111111":1,"111111111111111111111011111100111110001111000100001011":1,"111111111111111111111111111111000001110000001000000000":1,"111111111111111111111111111111100001111000001100001011":4,"111111111111111111111111111111111111111111001100001011":2,"111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111":3}],"billed_seconds_reported":1,"observables":[{"label":"kim_theta_0.0pi","x":0,"ideal":1,"measured":0.0434074074074074},{"label":"kim_theta_0.2pi","x":0.2,"ideal":0.4456058300201863,"measured":-0.02785185185185185},{"label":"kim_theta_0.35pi","x":0.35,"ideal":0.10168305520311371,"measured":-0.017185185185185185},{"label":"kim_theta_0.5pi","x":0.5,"ideal":0,"measured":-0.014814814814814817}],"values":{"rescaled_02":-0.6416382252559727,"rescaled_035":-0.3959044368600683,"rescaled_05":-0.34129692832764513},"circuit_facts":[{"label":"kim_theta_0.0pi","cz_count":249,"measured_qubits":["QB1","QB2","QB3","QB4","QB5","QB6","QB7","QB8","QB9","QB10","QB11","QB12","QB13","QB14","QB15","QB16","QB17","QB18","QB19","QB20","QB21","QB22","QB23","QB24","QB25","QB26","QB27","QB28","QB29","QB30","QB31","QB32","QB33","QB34","QB35","QB36","QB37","QB38","QB39","QB40","QB41","QB42","QB43","QB44","QB45","QB46","QB47","QB48","QB49","QB50","QB51","QB52","QB53","QB54"]},{"label":"kim_theta_0.2pi","cz_count":249,"measured_qubits":["QB1","QB2","QB3","QB4","QB5","QB6","QB7","QB8","QB9","QB10","QB11","QB12","QB13","QB14","QB15","QB16","QB17","QB18","QB19","QB20","QB21","QB22","QB23","QB24","QB25","QB26","QB27","QB28","QB29","QB30","QB31","QB32","QB33","QB34","QB35","QB36","QB37","QB38","QB39","QB40","QB41","QB42","QB43","QB44","QB45","QB46","QB47","QB48","QB49","QB50","QB51","QB52","QB53","QB54"]},{"label":"kim_theta_0.35pi","cz_count":249,"measured_qubits":["QB1","QB2","QB3","QB4","QB5","QB6","QB7","QB8","QB9","QB10","QB11","QB12","QB13","QB14","QB15","QB16","QB17","QB18","QB19","QB20","QB21","QB22","QB23","QB24","QB25","QB26","QB27","QB28","QB29","QB30","QB31","QB32","QB33","QB34","QB35","QB36","QB37","QB38","QB39","QB40","QB41","QB42","QB43","QB44","QB45","QB46","QB47","QB48","QB49","QB50","QB51","QB52","QB53","QB54"]},{"label":"kim_theta_0.5pi","cz_count":249,"measured_qubits":["QB1","QB2","QB3","QB4","QB5","QB6","QB7","QB8","QB9","QB10","QB11","QB12","QB13","QB14","QB15","QB16","QB17","QB18","QB19","QB20","QB21","QB22","QB23","QB24","QB25","QB26","QB27","QB28","QB29","QB30","QB31","QB32","QB33","QB34","QB35","QB36","QB37","QB38","QB39","QB40","QB41","QB42","QB43","QB44","QB45","QB46","QB47","QB48","QB49","QB50","QB51","QB52","QB53","QB54"]}],"answer":"I ran the experiment as 2 jobs on emerald:mock. Each job had 4 circuits with 250 shots per circuit. Nothing went to a real QPU, so no credits were spent. Job 01a16483-11d8-73d3-8e12-f5d0f53c437b was the test run. Job 01a16483-7eef-709f-b183-a03ccb413da6 was the stand-in for real emerald. The API reports 1.0 billed second for the final job. Mock jobs cost 0 credits.\n\nHow the circuits were built: I read the 83 CZ couplers that real emerald currently lists (calibration set 3a1a9ad0-0c98-49db-8cf5-7623d13729f4). I wrote each circuit straight in IQM's native gates, so no compiler could add, merge, or remove gates. The gate RZZ(-pi/2) = exp(i pi/4 ZZ) equals exactly one CZ plus a Z rotation on each of its 2 qubits, up to a global phase. I applied those Z rotations in software by shifting the phase of the next RX pulse. Each circuit has 3 steps, and each step has 54 RX gates and 83 CZ gates. That gives 249 CZ gates per circuit, one per coupler per step. Every circuit measures all 54 qubits. I read the circuits back from the server, and they match what I sent exactly.\n\nIdeal magnetization, computed without noise for these exact circuits: 1.000 at theta = 0, 0.446 at 0.2 pi, 0.102 at 0.35 pi, and 0.000 at 0.5 pi. This is the melting you asked to see. With no sideways field, all the spins stay up. As the field gets stronger, the spins tip over and the average drops toward zero.\n\nMeasured magnetization from the final mock job: 0.043, -0.028, -0.017, and -0.015. The mock machine returns random bits that do not depend on the circuit, so these numbers are close to zero for every theta. They show nothing about the physics. The noise-corrected values divide by the theta = 0 value, which is 0.043 here. They are rescaled_02 = -0.64, rescaled_035 = -0.40, and rescaled_05 = -0.34. Those numbers are meaningless, because dividing by a number near zero blows up the random noise. On real emerald, the theta = 0 circuit would read a little below 1 because of gate and readout errors. Dividing by it would then correct for part of that error. That correction works best when errors shrink every circuit's signal by about the same factor.\n\nCould a laptop have computed this? Yes. My laptop computed the exact ideal values in seconds. After 3 steps, each qubit's result depends only on qubits within 3 couplers of it, which is a few dozen qubits at most. The CZ-type gates are also simple to track exactly. So these circuits are classically easy, even though they use 54 qubits. This is not a quantum advantage. It would not be one even on the real QPU. A claim of advantage would need circuits that no classical method can simulate, such as many more steps, and results checked against the best classical methods. This run shows the principle of a quantum simulation: a field that does not commute with the spin coupling scrambles the ordered state, and the magnetization melts as the field grows.\n\nFiles are in /Users/claytonchancey/Desktop/quantum/.claude/worktrees/wf_8d7e6233-d69-9/kim/ (build.py, analyze.py, circuits.json, ideals.json, and the result JSON files). Both job IDs are in /Users/claytonchancey/Desktop/quantum/.claude/worktrees/wf_8d7e6233-d69-9/job_log.txt."}
